# Notice board is now backed by Firebase Firestore.
# Configuration is handled via lib/firebase_options.dart (generated by
# the FlutterFire CLI from project: daily-utility-1d724).
#
# No API keys are required here — Firestore security rules control who
# can read/write the `notice` collection.
#
# To publish a notice: open the Firebase console → Firestore → `notice`
# collection → Add document and fill in these fields:
#
#   title     string   (required) — headline
#   para      string   (required) — body / description
#   imgurl    string   (optional) — image URL shown at the top of the card
#   linkurl   string   (optional) — "Read more" button URL
#   createdAt timestamp(optional) — used for newest-first sorting
#   isPinned  bool     (optional) — pins the notice above all others
